00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:05.910 align:start position:0%
after years of waiting the mood in  indonesia's people's representative  council was one of celebration  there's no place for sexual violence  house speaker puan maharani declared as  legislators passed a highly anticipated  bill into law which aims to create a  better legal framework for victims of  sexual abuse to secure justice  this law is so important all these years  there were so many victims who didn't  get justice  they endured trauma they were  criminalized and victimized  the law has been broadly welcomed by  rights groups around the country for  making the well-being of sexual abuse  victims a priority by offering  compensation and other support  there are many breakthroughs in this law  in the best interest of the victims  it also expands the definition of sexual  crimes to include different types of  abuse  firstly and foremost it actually  regulates sexual crimes or sexual  violence that previously are not  considered as criminal acts or  partially regulated  which includes sexual harassment  passing the bill wasn't easy supporters  faced a strong challenge from those who  are opposed to such laws  the bill had faced some backlash since  its early stages which caused delays in  getting it passed conservative political  parties and some religious groups were  against it saying it will encourage  adultery and sex outside  marriage bill was in jeopardy people  were saying it supports free sex and  opens the door for sexual deviants but  it was proven that narrative was not  true  several high-profile cases helped keep  the issue in public focus  last month a dean at a university in  northern indonesia was acquitted of all  charges after a female student said he  sexually harassed her  her lawyer said he welcomes the new  legislation  under the law a letter from a  psychologist can be used as evidence i  hope going forward no more perpetrators  of sexual violence will be set free  students at the university have held  regular rallies in support of the  student who made the allegations  like many they say they just want their  campus and the rest of indonesia to be a  safer place  jessica washington al jazeera jakarta
 

